# Demo requests for the Mortgage Applications API (VS Code REST Client, Rider or Visual Studio).
# Start the API first: dotnet run --project src/MortgageApplications.Api
# Development only: the OpenAPI document is at /openapi/v1.json and the Scalar UI at /scalar.
# Every /api/ request needs a bearer token. The launch profiles set DevAuth__Enabled=true, so POST /dev/token issues
# one (Development only). Run the two token requests first; tokens last 15 minutes and die when the API stops.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5227

### Health (anonymous)
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### Get a token for alice (used by every request below)
# @name token
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "alice"
}

### Get a token for bob (used by the cross-user request at the end)
# @name bobToken
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "subject": "bob"
}

### Create an application (golden example E1: expected Approved)
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "annualIncome": 85000.00,
  "monthlyExpenses": 900.00,
  "depositAmount": 60000.00,
  "propertyValue": 300000.00,
  "termYears": 30
}

### Get it back (the id comes from the response above)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}

### Start an assessment (202 Accepted, status Pending; the Location header points at the assessment)
# @name assess
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.id}}/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}

### Poll the assessment: always 200. Repeat until status is Completed (with the result) or Failed (with failedAt)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.id}}/assessments/{{assess.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}

### Create a high-LTV application (golden example E2: deposit 20,000, expected Declined on LTV)
# @name createDeclined
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "annualIncome": 85000.00,
  "monthlyExpenses": 900.00,
  "depositAmount": 20000.00,
  "propertyValue": 300000.00,
  "termYears": 30
}

### Assess it: still 202, and it completes as Declined (a result, not an error)
# @name assessDeclined
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{createDeclined.response.body.id}}/assessments
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}

### Poll it until status is Completed; result.decision is Declined
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{createDeclined.response.body.id}}/assessments/{{assessDeclined.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}

### Invalid input: 400 ValidationProblemDetails naming termYears
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "annualIncome": 85000.00,
  "monthlyExpenses": 900.00,
  "depositAmount": 60000.00,
  "propertyValue": 300000.00,
  "termYears": 50
}

### Loan below the 1,000 minimum: 400 naming depositAmount
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "annualIncome": 85000.00,
  "monthlyExpenses": 900.00,
  "depositAmount": 299500.00,
  "propertyValue": 300000.00,
  "termYears": 30
}

### Unknown property (an attempt to set the owner): 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/applications
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "annualIncome": 85000.00,
  "monthlyExpenses": 900.00,
  "depositAmount": 60000.00,
  "propertyValue": 300000.00,
  "termYears": 30,
  "ownerId": "someone-else"
}

### Unknown id: 404 ProblemDetails
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/0193a8f2-0000-7000-8000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token.response.body.token}}

### Another user: bob asks for alice's application and gets the same 404 as an unknown id (no existence leak)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/applications/{{create.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bobToken.response.body.token}}
